# secrets + personal state stay OFF the repo
bot/.env
bot/data/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-08-16: the churning state files moved out of the root into _data/.
# The WHOLE folder is user state - chat buses, journal, usage, the 20s snapshot,
# config.json, memory.md, schedule.json, staged-trade.json. One line covers all
# of it, and anything new that lands in there is ignored by default rather than
# by someone remembering to add a line. The shipped config default is
# _app/config.default.json, which IS tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
_data/
# Bare-name copies, kept so an older checkout or a stray write at the root is
# still ignored rather than silently staged.
chat-inbox.jsonl
chat-outbox.jsonl
journal.jsonl
usage.jsonl
memory.md
# YOUR trading plan. Seeded from RULES.template.md on first run, then yours.
# Shipping this would hand every user someone else's strategy as if it were
# the app's opinion, and an update would overwrite what they wrote.
RULES.md
saved-workbenches/
panels/*
!panels/00-welcome.html
__pycache__/
*.pyc
bot-src.tgz
nohup.out

# raw screen captures are huge (60MB+ per take) - only the cut MP4 ships
demo/raw/
demo/audio/

# Claude Code per-machine tool allowlist - private, machine-specific.
# LEADING ** MATTERS: a pattern containing a slash is anchored to the repo
# root, so the old `.claude/settings.local.json` did not cover _app/.claude/
# and it showed up as a new untracked file after the 2026-08-16 split.
**/.claude/settings.local.json

# live snapshot - regenerated every 20s, machine-specific
state.json

# TradingView captures - personal, regenerated on demand
tv-shots/

# desktop build output (build.py) + shell runtime state
dist/
build/
webview-data/
logs/
bot/.env.bak*

#Extra research into trading 
research/

# personal trading playbooks - not product
BRAIN-*.md
# The per-lane brains. Same reason as BRAIN-*.md and RULES.md: this is HIS strategy,
# and shipping it would hand every user someone else's playbook as if it were the
# app's opinion. Templates live in TheTradingBrains/_templates/ and DO ship.
TheTradingBrains/*
!TheTradingBrains/_templates/
staged-trade.json
# scheduler state: YOUR cadence plus last_run_ts. Shipping it would hand a
# new user someone else's schedule AND a timestamp the due-check reads, so
# their first scan would look already-run.
schedule.json

# personal agent-lane charter - how ONE person works, not product
.claude/SCOPED-SPACE-RULES.md

# video cut rigs: big binaries, and the source captures can contain live keys.
# Publishing a cut is a separate, deliberate decision.
demo/edit-*/

# third-party tools cloned locally (see _tools/README.md) - never ours to ship
_tools/*
!_tools/README.md
